  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that multiprofile RNA modeling with scvi_n200 substantially outperforms singleprofile RNA models, and transformer aggregation is slightly better than avgpool for scvi_n200. The key uncertainty is whether this multiprofile gain is specific to scvi_n200 or also applies to simpler PCA representations. config_003 tests pca_n2000 under the same multiprofile + transformer setting as the current best RNA-only model, directly isolating the effect of RNA representation while also clarifying whether multiprofile helps PCA. This is a high-value, low-complexity next step because it avoids introducing image modality or fusion before the RNA-side design choices are better understood."
